el">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="katex-base"><span class="katex-strut" style="height:1.0361em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;"></span><span class="minner"><span class="mopen delimcenter" style="top:0em;">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right:0.0359em;">g</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height:0.3361em;"><span style="top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height:2.7em;"></span><span class="katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right:0.0315em;">k</span><span class="mpunct mtight">,</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right:0.0572em;">j</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height:0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right:0.0077em;">R</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">Q</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height:0.3361em;"><span style="top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height:2.7em;"></span><span class="katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right:0.0315em;">k</span><span class="mpunct mtight">,</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right:0.0572em;">j</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height:0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose delimcenter" style="top:0em;">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>8:[[["$","link","css:/assets/index-DStW-UAj.css",{"rel":"stylesheet","precedence":"vite-rsc/importer-resources","href":"/assets/index-DStW-UAj.css","data-rsc-css-href":"/assets/index-DStW-UAj.css"}],"$undefined"],["$","section",null,{"className":"_section_r7ckf_27","id":"current-distribution","data-paper-section":true,"aria-labelledby":"current-distribution-title","children":[["$","header",null,{"className":"_sectionHead_r7ckf_28","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"2"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"id":"current-distribution-title","children":"Current joint-distribution construction"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Current forecasting preserves historical joint asset movements, expresses each algorithm as probabilistic views, and combines their probability adjustments rather than averaging point forecasts."}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"_sectionContent_r7ckf_32","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"At the current request time, Joint Probability Distribution asks Weight Optimization for weights specific to the complete request identity and asks Algorithm for each algorithm’s conclusion over the same universe, reference time, and horizon. Algorithm obtains a separate Evidence Bundle for each method. Algorithm Data Collection places exact FSC and DART values in an Exact Data Plane, encodes narrative material once with a common encoder, and packages both representations for the relevant algorithm decoder. Each decoder and prediction function is owned by Algorithm, not by data collection."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"An algorithm conclusion is a collection of probabilistic views, not a point forecast with a separate confidence score. A view pairs a deterministic target function of the asset-return vector with its predicted quantile function. The target may describe one asset, a relative return, or a basket. Common probability levels make views comparable; uncertainty is represented by quantile width and shape, while relative trust between algorithms is represented by calibrated weights."}],[[["$","link","css:/assets/index-DStW-UAj.css",{"rel":"stylesheet","precedence":"vite-rsc/importer-resources","href":"/assets/index-DStW-UAj.css","data-rsc-css-href":"/assets/index-DStW-UAj.css"}],"$undefined"],["$","figure",null,{"className":"_equation_r7ckf_37","aria-label":"Algorithm conclusion contract","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"math-render","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$12"}}],"$L13"]}],"$L14"]}]],"$L15","$L16","$L17","$L18"]}]]}]]
